    <class name="Screen"
           c:symbol-prefix="screen"
           c:type="WPEScreen"
           parent="GObject.Object"
           abstract="1"
           glib:type-name="WPEScreen"
           glib:get-type="wpe_screen_get_type"
           glib:type-struct="ScreenClass">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="Source/WebKit/WPEPlatform/wpe/WPEScreen.cpp"
           line="42">A monitor connected to a [class@Display].

[class@Screen] is an abstract class that platform implementations derive to
represent a monitor. Enumerate the screens of a display with
[method@Display.get_n_screens] and [method@Display.get_screen].

A screen exposes its position, size, physical size, scale and refresh rate,
and provides a [class@ScreenSyncObserver] to be notified on vertical sync.</doc>
      <source-position filename="Source/WebKit/WPEPlatform/wpe/WPEScreen.h"
                       line="50"/>
      <virtual-method name="get_sync_observer" invoker="get_sync_observer">
